# Graphify knowledge-graph working files. GRAPH_REPORT.md is un-ignored below so the map of
# the project is versioned alongside the code it describes and its diffs are readable in
# review. graph.json and graph.html are not: they are rebuildable indexes of 5 MB each that
# rewrite wholesale on every sync, so versioning them would grow history by megabytes per
# commit while adding nothing a reviewer can read. Rebuild with `graphify` -- the extraction
# cache under graphify-out/cache/ means a rebuild re-reads, it does not re-pay for the LLM.
# The pattern must glob the contents rather than name the directory: git does not descend
# into an excluded directory, so `!` on a file inside one never takes effect.
graphify-out/*
!graphify-out/GRAPH_REPORT.md

# Campaign working files: a 54 MB third-party corpus index and a symlink into the
# cluster image tree. The corpus is pinned in the report by name and digest, not by
# being republished here.
examples/*/corpus.jsonl
examples/*/media

# local scan cache for tools/check_no_secrets.py -- content digests, no content
.ascep-secretscan-cache.json
